{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:0.2", "PA_ja_34:0.3"], "en": "The First Book, Chapter on the Bird’s Nest (Kulāvakavagga)", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:0.4"], "en": "4. The Fish Jātaka:", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:1.1"], "en": "“Cold does not trouble me, nor heat;", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:1.2"], "en": "the net does not distress me.”", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:1.3"], "en": "\"And as for him whom that fish-wife imagines to be me,", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:1.4"], "en": "he has gone elsewhere for pleasure.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"},
{"segs": ["PA_ja_34:2.1"], "en": "Thus ends the fourth Jātaka, the Maccha-jātaka.", "model": "mitra-v4", "translated_at": "2026-11-27T12:48:33Z"}
